                <pb facs="0713" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg615"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that Mr. Geldart says his shipment by the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mashona</hi>, including necessary charges, would be covered by $1,000, and
                    that $575 would cover his shipment by the <hi rendition="#italic">Beatrice</hi>.
                    If better terms can not be had, however, he will accept the British offer.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
